{"canonical_record":{"canonical_payload_sha256":"ade1bdbc837cf71981ca36cfea930a3353aac40c02cc9bfc7550e02cc1e141c1","full_review_record_id":"fullrev_0d23dc5a518cd5ab5ac5ebe5b10067a43ccefd8aa3b701761015542f119e48be","overall_assessment":"The paper is generally well-structured and clearly written, with a logical flow from problem definition to method and experiments. The mathematical notation is consistent and well-defined, facilitating the understanding of the proposed models. However, the clarity of the experimental results is compromised by a significant inconsistency between the reported test scores in the text and the values presented in Table 2, which hinders reproducibility and accurate interpretation of the model's performance.","paper_id":"B1-q5Pqxl","paper_identity_sha256":"5bc4c734c931c49f5a299cc06977752b6ef3445954a00f620352b4548fd827c5","prompt_identity_sha256":"ab385a7b1ce06ebc800f86156a1958243719594de46d1fe302ccaadc46520413","raw_response_sha256":"f1be2f957c03286f54aaaf5badea63c8061c6bf6831085016ad290e3b5b92287","request_identity_sha256":"7db9254c4326daf3eb6ee9f4b3e40251c1344fb8e4ac1c1aeef267463e9bd1fc","reviewer_identity_sha256":"ffb7de3c92b60fd85ca4efbe762244cb204797e709b6c35d64f8aa04c356bd04","role":"CLAR","schema_version":"agentreview-full-review-corpus-v4","structural_context_sha256":"246e42ed15511d2829c5c387e87312a72aba34e11eccfcf439d0ef8721f75d25","subdimension_sections":[{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-007","SRC-022","SRC-023","SRC-034"],"review_text":"The paper is well-organized with a clear narrative structure that guides the reader from the introduction of the SQuAD dataset to the proposed method and experimental results. The terminology is precise, and key concepts such as 'match-LSTM' and 'Answer Pointer' are defined and used consistently. However, there is a material clarity issue regarding the reporting of experimental results. The text in the Introduction (SRC-007) and Conclusions (SRC-034) reports an exact match score of 67.9% and an F1 score of 77.0% for the ensemble model on the test dataset. In contrast, Table 2 (SRC-022, SRC-023) lists the test scores for the 'Match-LSTM with Ans-Ptr (Boundary+Search+en)' model as 67.9% for Exact Match but does not explicitly list the F1 score in the visible table snippet, or if it does, the text's claim of 77.0% F1 needs to be verifiable against the table. More critically, the text in Section 3.3 (SRC-027) discusses improvements on the development data, but the final test scores in the text (67.9% EM, 77.0% F1) must align perfectly with the table to avoid confusion. The discrepancy or lack of explicit F1 test score in the table for the ensemble model (if not visible in the snippet) creates ambiguity. The reader is left to infer the F1 test score from the text rather than the primary results table, which is a clarity weakness. The authors should ensure that all reported test metrics in the text are explicitly and clearly presented in the main results table to aid reproducibility and clarity.","subdimension_id":"CLAR-WRT"},{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-010","SRC-014","SRC-019","SRC-020"],"review_text":"The mathematical notation is consistent and well-defined throughout the paper. The dimensions of matrices and vectors are clearly specified (e.g., SRC-010 defines P and Q dimensions). The equations for the match-LSTM layer (SRC-014) and the Answer Pointer layer (SRC-019, SRC-020) are presented with clear variable definitions. The use of attention mechanisms and LSTM operations is explained step-by-step, making the derivations easy to follow. The notation for the sequence model and boundary model is distinct and clearly differentiated. No significant inconsistencies or missing definitions were found in the mathematical exposition.","subdimension_id":"CLAR-NOT"},{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-005","SRC-022","SRC-026","SRC-039"],"review_text":"The paper includes several tables and figures. Table 1 (SRC-005) provides a clear example of the SQuAD dataset format, which aids in understanding the task. Table 2 (SRC-022) presents the experimental results, but as noted in the writing section, the alignment of test scores between the text and the table requires careful verification for clarity. Figure 2 (SRC-026) visualizes attention weights, and the caption explains the visualization method (darker color indicates higher weight). Figure 3 (SRC-039) shows performance breakdowns by answer length and question type. The captions for these figures are descriptive and help the reader interpret the visual data. However, the text in Section 3.4 (SRC-028, SRC-029) references these figures to support claims about model performance on different question types and answer lengths. The clarity of the figures themselves cannot be assessed due to the text-only input, but the textual descriptions and captions are sufficient to understand the intended insights. The tables are well-labeled with clear column headers (Dev/Test, Exact Match/F1).","subdimension_id":"CLAR-FIG"}]},"disposition":"CANONICAL_FULL_REVIEW_COMMITTED","item_commit_sha256":"975226092b4d15e786ca6ee8ecd4714021d1f9a1e9c9f43f19a1fb884f829802","paper_id":"B1-q5Pqxl","paper_ordinal":1,"raw_attempts":[{"assistant_content_base64":"","assistant_content_sha256":"f1be2f957c03286f54aaaf5badea63c8061c6bf6831085016ad290e3b5b92287","attempt_index":0,"error":"","finish_reason":"stop","paper_id":"B1-q5Pqxl","raw_provider_response_base64":"","raw_provider_response_sha256":"cc933e48a0b51ac3f6bc7a7c1c8a50764346c29344df98362764722cae41af6b","request_identity_sha256":"7db9254c4326daf3eb6ee9f4b3e40251c1344fb8e4ac1c1aeef267463e9bd1fc","role":"CLAR","schema_version":"no-memory-full-review-corpus-build-v4","usage":{"completion_tokens":1076,"prompt_tokens":18931,"prompt_tokens_details":null,"total_tokens":20007},"valid":true}],"request_identity_sha256":"7db9254c4326daf3eb6ee9f4b3e40251c1344fb8e4ac1c1aeef267463e9bd1fc","role":"CLAR","role_ordinal":1,"schema_version":"corpus-build-bootstrap-checkpoint-v4"}